Robert Huebner (rhuebner@sage.cc.purdue.edu) wrote:
: In article <1993Feb1.192151.28833@ultb.isc.rit.edu> kdc5072@ultb.isc.rit.edu (K.D. Colagio) writes:
: >Not wure if this is a bug, or a mistake that happened when I was
: >compiling (because I had to modify to compile) but here goes...
: >
: >Now, when I drink a potion of object detection or gold detection, they
: >stay on the screen...is this right?  I thought they disappeared when the
: >effects of the potion wore off (and you could see the coridor around you
: >again...i.e. you hit any key...)

: This happens on my version as well (Amiga, self-compiled).  However,
: the  Monster Detection (at least on mine) is sort of the opposite extreme-
: after casting or quaffing I see the monsters on the level for only a brief
: half-second and then they're gone.  Obviously a bug as no useful info
: can be gained in the short time before it disappears.  Perhaps this was
: a compile bug (SAS 6.1 is what I used).

No.  I don't think its a bug in either case.  The detection behavior is
just being consistant with normal sight behavior.  If you see an object or
some money, they always stay on the map, even after they are out of your
line of site.  Monsters on the other hand do not.  Its called
consistancy.  Nethack 3.0j wasn't consistant with the regard to objects
and gold, but was for monsters.  So if anything it was a bugfix, not a
bug.

